Stock decrement runs outside the order's transaction.

reserve() sends its UPDATE through the connection pool instead of the
transaction it was given. Each decrement autocommits on its own connection,
so when a later line of the same order is out of stock and the transaction
rolls back, the earlier lines' stock stays taken: the order is gone but the
units never come back. Compiles, and every single-line happy path still
works.

Expect-Fail: TestRejectedOrderLeavesNoTrace
Expect-Fail: TestUnknownProductRejectedAtomically

